      "reasoning": "Excellent! Turn 3 main phase. Vial is at 2 counters. I drew another Broadside Bombardiers. Let me plan:\n\
\n\
**Board state:**\n\
- Me: Aether Vial (2 counters), Bloodstained Mire, Wasteland\n\
- Opponent: Island (tapped), Underground Sea (untapped) - they're on UB\n\
\n\
**My plan this turn:**\n\
1. Play Wasteland (land drop) - now I have 2 Wastelands + Bloodstained Mire\n\
2. Wasteland their Underground Sea to cut them off black mana\n\
3. Crack Bloodstained Mire for a Mountain\n\
4. Cast Broadside Bombardiers (2R) with Mountain + Wasteland colorless + Wasteland colorless... wait, Broadside Bombardiers costs {2}{R}. I need 1R + 2 generic. If I sac a Wasteland to destroy Underground Sea, I lose a land. Let me think...\n\
\n\
Actually, better sequencing:\n\
1. Play Wasteland from hand (land #3)\n\
2. Use old Wasteland to destroy Underground Sea (sac it)\n\
3. Crack Bloodstained Mire for a Mountain\n\
4. Now I have: Mountain + new Wasteland = 1R + 1C = only 2 mana. Broadside Bombardiers costs 2R (3 total). Not enough.\n\
\n\
Alternative: Don't Wasteland yet, cast Broadside Bombardiers instead.\n\
1. Play Wasteland from hand\n\
2. Crack Bloodstained Mire for Mountain\n\
3. Now I have Mountain + Wasteland + Wasteland = R + C + C = 3 mana, cast Broadside Bombardiers for {2}{R}\n\
\n\
That gives me a 2/2 menace haste attacker! And I keep my original Wasteland to threaten Underground Sea. Even better.\n\
\n\
Let me do this plan. First, play the Wasteland from hand.",
