      "reasoning": "Turn 4 main phase. I drew another Aether Vial. Let me think about the best play:\n\
\n\
**My board:** Aether Vial (2 counters), Badlands, 2x Wasteland\n\
**Opponent:** Orcish Bowmasters (1/1), Orc Army (2/2), Underground Sea (tapped), Island (tapped) - both summoning sick\n\
**Opponent at 10 life, me at 19**\n\
\n\
**Options:**\n\
1. Cast Broadside Bombardiers (2R) - haste menace 2/2, can attack right away\n\
2. Vial in Munitions Expert to kill Bowmasters (1 damage with 1 goblin on the field... wait, I have NO goblins on the battlefield currently, so Expert would deal 0 damage plus itself = 1 damage after it enters. Actually it says \"equal to the number of Goblins you control\" - Expert is a Goblin, so after it enters it counts itself = 1 damage. That kills Bowmasters!)\n\
3. Wasteland Underground Sea\n\
4. Cast second Aether Vial\n\
\n\
Actually, the best sequence:\n\
1. Vial in Munitions Expert (2 CMV) to kill Bowmasters - Expert deals 1 damage (counting itself). This removes Bowmasters trigger from punishing my draws.\n\
2. Then cast Broadside Bombardiers (2R) with Badlands + 2 Wastelands\n\
3. Attack with both Bombardiers (2/2 menace haste) and Expert (1/1) - opponent has only the 2/2 Orc Army to block, can't block menace with 1 creature\n\
\n\
Wait, but if I Vial in Expert, then cast Bombardiers, opponent's Bowmasters is dead. They have just the 2/2 Orc Army. I attack with Bombardiers (menace, needs 2 blockers) and Expert. They can block Expert with the Army token, but Bombardiers gets through for 2. Or they let everything through for 3.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me reconsider. Should I save the Vial activation for a more critical moment? The opponent's lands are all tapped, and they only have 2 cards in hand. They already used 2 Force of Wills. The Bowmasters will get value every time I draw extra cards.\n\
\n\
Let me kill Bowmasters now with Vial + Expert, then cast Bombardiers and attack.\n\
\n\
First, activate Aether Vial to put Munitions Expert onto the battlefield:",
