      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Flooded Strand over Underground Sea on turn 1 is slightly suboptimal. The player has Ponder in hand which costs {U}, and they want to cast it this turn. Playing Underground Sea directly would allow casting Ponder without paying 1 life to crack the fetch land. Flooded Strand will need to be cracked (costing 1 life) to fetch an Island/Plains to cast Ponder, and since the only fetchable blue source in the deck is likely Underground Sea itself, they're paying 1 life unnecessarily. Additionally, playing Underground Sea preserves the fetch land for later use as shuffle effects (e.g., after Ponder) or for deck thinning at a more strategically valuable time.",
