    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Fetching Badlands instead of a basic Mountain exposes the land to the opponent's potential Wasteland effects. The reasoning even started to identify this concern but then pivoted to flexibility. With Aether Vial on 2 counters able to flash in Munitions Expert (the main BR card), and Broadside Bombardiers being the immediate cast needing R, a basic Mountain would have been safer. The opponent is playing a blue deck that could run Wasteland, and losing a land to Wasteland against a deck that's already mana-light would be devastating for casting Muxus or Goblin Ringleader.",
